IN THE HIGH COURT OF MADRAS
CASE NO: Criminal Revision No. 312 of 2021
CITATION: 2022 SCC OnLine Mad 410
YEAR: 2022

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: N. Anand Venkatesh

PARTIES:
State vs Cyber Phishing Accused

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Information Technology Act, 2000, Indian Penal Code, 1860

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 43 IT Act, Section 66C IT Act, Section 66D IT Act, Section 420 IPC

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
phishing, identity theft, cheating by personation, cyber fraud

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Affirmed the framing of charges under Sections 66C and 66D of the IT Act along with Section 420 IPC for orchestrating fraudulent spoofed banking portals to harvest login credentials.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 43 IT Act, Section 66C IT Act, Section 66D IT Act, Section 420 IPC.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

